00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,220
Listen to a talk in an archaeology class.

2
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:06,104
Man:

3
00:00:06,104 --> 00:00:14,162
For decades, archaeologists believed that complex societies and the monumental architecture, the large buildings

4
00:00:14,162 --> 00:00:17,730
signifying them, only emerged after agriculture,

5
00:00:17,730 --> 00:00:22,100
and that farming was essential for societal development.

6
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:27,624
After all, before agriculture developed, people tended not to settle in a single place,

7
00:00:27,624 --> 00:00:31,220
but moved from place to place in search of food.

8
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:36,110
We call such people nomadic hunter gatherers.

9
00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:41,000
They were continuously on the move to hunt and collect food.

10
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,953
And for people who aren't settled, it was more practical to live in small

11
00:00:45,953 --> 00:00:49,884
mobile groups rather than in complex societies.

12
00:00:49,884 --> 00:00:52,110
Or so it was believed.

13
00:00:52,110 --> 00:01:00,040
But the excavation of the ancient site of Gobekli Tepe threw a wrench in this whole story.

14
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:09,420
Gobekli Tepe, dating back about 11,000 years, consists of multiple massive pillars arranged in circles

15
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:14,110
and is considered the world's oldest known temple.

16
00:01:14,110 --> 00:01:29,180
Remarkably, it predates the earliest evidence of agriculture in the area by several thousand years.

17
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:38,180
This suggests spiritual practices, not agriculture, may have caused early communities to form.

18
00:01:38,180 --> 00:01:51,190
Many scholars interpret the site as a ceremonial center, a periodic gathering place for nomadic hunter gatherers.

19
00:01:51,190 --> 00:01:57,642
More recently, archaeologists there did find traces of things like food processing areas, stone

20
00:01:57,642 --> 00:02:02,250
tools for grinding grains, as well as actual plant residues

21
00:02:02,250 --> 00:02:10,292
Yet these residues come from local wild grains, not domesticated crops,

22
00:02:10,292 --> 00:02:16,140
and the structures may not indicate year-round habitation.

23
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:16,190
So while Gobekli Tepe might have hosted temporary gatherings, the evidence still supports the

24
00:02:16,190 --> 00:02:16,240
idea that spiritual practices played a central role in early societal development.
